Cite these when a screen is reported
Cite the tools whose screens you report. Author lists, journals and DOIs below were verified against PubMed on 2026-11-18, except ANARCII's, which is a preprint and is quoted from the citation block in the installed package's own metadata.

DeepSP — Kalejaye LA, Wu I-E, Terry T, Lai P-K. DeepSP: Deep learning-based spatial properties to predict monoclonal antibody stability. Comput Struct Biotechnol J 23:2220–2229 (2024). 10.1016/j.csbj.2024.05.029
DeepViscosity — Kalejaye LA, Chu J-M, Wu I-E, et al., Lai P-K. Accelerating high-concentration monoclonal antibody development with large-scale viscosity data and ensemble deep learning. mAbs 17(1):2483944 (2025). 10.1080/19420862.2025.2483944
ANARCII — Greenshields-Watson A, Agarwal P, Robinson SA, et al., Deane CM. ANARCII: A generalised language model for antigen receptor numbering. bioRxiv 2025.04.16.648720. 10.1101/2025.04.16.648720
AbLang-2 — Olsen TH, Moal IH, Deane CM. Addressing the antibody germline bias and its effect on language models for improved antibody design. Bioinformatics 40(11) (2024). 10.1093/bioinformatics/btae618
BioPhi and OASis — Prihoda D, Maamary J, Waight A, et al., Bitton DA. BioPhi: A platform for antibody design, humanization, and humanness evaluation based on natural antibody repertoires and deep learning. mAbs 14(1):2020203 (2022). 10.1080/19420862.2021.2020203
MHCflurry 2.0 — O'Donnell TJ, Rubinsteyn A, Laserson U. MHCflurry 2.0: Improved pan-allele prediction of MHC class I-presented peptides by incorporating antigen processing. Cell Syst 11(1):42–48.e7 (2020). 10.1016/j.cels.2020.06.010
IEDB — Vita R, Mahajan S, Overton JA, et al., Peters B. The Immune Epitope Database (IEDB): 2018 update. Nucleic Acids Res 47(D1):D339–D343 (2019). 10.1093/nar/gky1006
TEPITOPE — Sturniolo T, Bono E, Ding J, et al., Hammer J. Generation of tissue-specific and promiscuous HLA ligand databases using DNA microarrays and virtual HLA class II matrices. Nat Biotechnol 17(6):555–561 (1999). 10.1038/9858
DockQ v2 — Mirabello C, Wallner B. DockQ v2: improved automatic quality measure for protein multimers, nucleic acids, and small molecules. Bioinformatics 40(10) (2024). 10.1093/bioinformatics/btae586
ProLIF — Bouysset C, Fiorucci S. ProLIF: a library to encode molecular interactions as fingerprints. J Cheminform 13(1):72 (2021). 10.1186/s13321-021-00548-6
PoseBusters — Buttenschoen M, Morris GM, Deane CM. PoseBusters: AI-based docking methods fail to generate physically valid poses or generalise to novel sequences. Chem Sci 15(9):3130–3139 (2024). 10.1039/d3sc04185a
ADMET-AI — Swanson K, Walther P, Leitz J, et al., Zou J. ADMET-AI: a machine learning ADMET platform for evaluation of large-scale chemical libraries. Bioinformatics 40(7) (2024). 10.1093/bioinformatics/btae416
Chemprop — Heid E, Greenman KP, Chung Y, et al., McGill CJ. Chemprop: A machine learning package for chemical property prediction. J Chem Inf Model 64(1):9–17 (2024). 10.1021/acs.jcim.3c01250
ThermoMPNN — Dieckhaus H, Brocidiacono M, Randolph NZ, Kuhlman B. Transfer learning to leverage larger datasets for improved prediction of protein stability changes. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA 121(6):e2314853121 (2024). 10.1073/pnas.2314853121
MMseqs2 — Steinegger M, Söding J. MMseqs2 enables sensitive protein sequence searching for the analysis of massive data sets. Nat Biotechnol 35(11):1026–1028 (2017). 10.1038/nbt.3988
Foldseek — van Kempen M, Kim SS, Tumescheit C, et al., Steinegger M. Fast and accurate protein structure search with Foldseek. Nat Biotechnol 42(2):243–246 (2024). 10.1038/s41587-023-01773-0
